{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":488923,"name":"OliG","username":"OliG","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/o/b4bc9f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T12:02:21.271Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHi,\u003cbr\u003e\nI’m having a persistent issue with Grok Bot on Windows 10.\u003cbr\u003e\nDetails:\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot version: 0.30.0 (Stable channel)\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: Windows 10\u003cbr\u003e\nThe problem started this morning after a Windows update.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat happened:\u003cbr\u003e\nAfter the Windows update, Grok Bot lost connection to the Agent Computer.\u003cbr\u003e\nI tried signing out and back in multiple times.\u003cbr\u003e\nAt some point the app showed a white screen with a black loading dot.\u003cbr\u003e\nAfter clearing local data and relaunching, my bots reappeared in the sidebar.\u003cbr\u003e\nHowever, the computer remains unreachable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrent status:\u003cbr\u003e\nMy bots are visible again.\u003cbr\u003e\nI get the message: “Can’t reach Grok Bot’s Computer. Your Bots, files and logins are safe. If it doesn’t reconnect on its own, recover Grok Bot’s computer to keep the data.”\u003cbr\u003e\nWhen I click Recover, it fails with:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Recovery failed. The recovery couldn’t finish; Grok Bot’s computer may still be inaccessible. Your Bots, files and logins are safe.”\u003cbr\u003e\n“Update Agent Computer” button is grayed out.\u003cbr\u003e\nChecking for app updates also fails with a connection error (“Unable to check for updates. Check your connection and try again.”).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I already tried:\u003cbr\u003e\nFully quitting the app + killing all processes\u003cbr\u003e\nSigning out / signing back in several times\u003cbr\u003e\nChanging DNS to 1.1.1.1 / 8.8.8.8 + flushing DNS\u003cbr\u003e\nTesting with mobile hotspot\u003cbr\u003e\nAttempting Recover (failed)\u003cbr\u003e\nClearing local AppData folder\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy bots, files and logins appear to be safe, but I cannot reconnect to the shared computer.\u003cbr\u003e\nCould you please check the status of my Agent Computer on your side and perform a manual recovery if needed?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThank you!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteps to Reproduce:\u003cbr\u003e\n1.I performed a Windows 10 update this morning.\u003cbr\u003e\n2. After the update, Grok Bot (version 0.30.0) lost connection to the Agent Computer.\u003cbr\u003e\n3. I signed out and signed back in multiple times.\u003cbr\u003e\n4. The app sometimes showed a white screen with a black loading dot.\u003cbr\u003e\n5. After clearing the local AppData folder and relaunching, my bots reappeared in the sidebar.\u003cbr\u003e\n6.However, the computer remains unreachable.\u003cbr\u003e\n7. I get the error: “Can’t reach Grok Bot’s Computer. Your Bots, files and logins are safe…”\u003cbr\u003e\n8. Clicking Recover fails with: “Recovery failed. The recovery couldn’t finish; Grok Bot’s computer may still be inaccessible. Your Bots, files and logins are safe.”\u003cbr\u003e\n9. “Update Agent Computer” button is grayed out.\u003cbr\u003e\n10. Checking for updates also fails with a connection error.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.30.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T12:02:28.806Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":41.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171344,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible","display_username":"OliG","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137314,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible/171344/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":489484,"name":"OliG","username":"